#
# Look-alikes for tools/release/redaction-scan.py (read by default).
# action | class | path glob | regex | reason
# action: drop (a look-alike, not counted) or info (listed, not a finding).
# class `*` is any class; the glob is fnmatch over the whole path ("*"
# matches across "/"); the regex is searched in the line and drops or lists
# the hits its match overlaps.  Patterns and public names only: a private
# value (login, lab, runner or bridge host, address) never goes here.
#
# Placeholders (docs/release/redaction-audit.md part 3).
drop | home-path | * | /(home|Users)/\.\.\. | elided path, not a user name
drop | login-at-host | * | root@BOARD\b | placeholder for the board's ssh target
drop | login-at-host | * | root@localhost\b | loopback through a tunnel
drop | login-at-host | tools/mali/panthor/tests/board_lock.rs | root[@]board-lock-test\b | test fixture for the lock's BOARD_HOST
drop | * | * | <(user|login)@(host|board)> | placeholder
# The RFC 1918 fixtures that the console redaction self-test rewrites.
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/board_selftest.sh | \b(10\.11\.12\.(1|13)|172\.16\.0\.9)\b | redact_dir fixture input (RFC 1918)
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/pr-session-selftest.sh | secret-user@10\.9\.8\.7\b | fixture of the self-test's BOARD_HOST refusal
# The preflight selftest's fake BOARD_UART canary (a look-alike, never a real value).
drop | password | tools/cts/imx8mp-gles3-preflight-selftest.sh | SECRET\=ttyUSB | selftest fixture: the fake UART string the test asserts the preflight never prints
# Product defaults and keywords.
drop | som-serial | * | verdin-(am62p|imx8mp)-00000000 | zeroed serial: the product's default host name
drop | password | * | NOPASSWD: | sudoers keyword, not a password
drop | lab-host | * | \barmadillo\.local\b | the vendor's mDNS default host name
drop | lab-host | * | \byakogl-gate\b | the gate's public runner label
drop | lab-host | * | \bccfarm\b | the name of the farm tool
# The generated i.MX8MP register header (tools/hal-nxp/gen_regs.py, NXP's
# names): a lab host's name is also the prefix of some PHY power-domain
# identifiers.  Only the uppercase prefix with its `_PHY` suffix in that one
# file; the bare name stays a finding there too.
drop | lab-host | driver/rust/src/soc/imx8mp/regs.rs | (?<![A-Za-z0-9])[A-Z]{3}[0-9]_PHY(?![A-Za-z0-9]) | NXP register identifier (a PHY's power-domain field) in a generated file, not a host name
# tools/env/* drives the pool and image tool through its public interface:
# its CLI (`<tool> image build`, `<tool> pool apply`, `<tool> login`, `command
# -v <tool>`), its environment variables (`<TOOL>_RECIPES`, `<TOOL>_URL`), a
# session, CLI or pool of it, and its server's docs (`<tool>-complex`).
drop | lab-host | tools/env/* | \b[A-Za-z]+ (image|pool|login|session|CLI)\b|\bcommand -v [A-Za-z]+\b|\b[A-Z]+_(RECIPES|URL)\b|\b[A-Za-z]+-complex\b | the pool and image tool's CLI, environment variables, pools and server docs
# A compiled pattern bound to a name that contains "secret", not a value.
drop | password | *.py | \bSECRET\s*=\s*re\.compile\( | a regex named SECRET (the leak pattern a checker searches for)
# The scanner's self-description: lab-layout mentions in its own class table and pattern.
drop | lab-layout | tools/release/redaction-scan.py | \$HOME/com/github/|yakogl\-in\-rust | the class's own name, in the file that defines the class
# E-mail shapes that are no address of a person.
drop | * | * | @[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.invalid\b | .invalid placeholder (RFC 2606)
drop | email | * | \bt@example\.org\b | a self-test's address
drop | email | * | \bgit@github\.com\b | the project's clone URL
drop | email | tools/testdata/* | @fa10000\.bootdev\.part_ | U-Boot device node in a console capture
drop | email | tools/testdata/* | @1000\.service\b | systemd unit name in a console capture
drop | email | docs/notes/pre-study-iq9075.md | @oss\.qualcomm\.com\b | Message-ID of an upstream patch series
# Upstream authors (information, not a finding).
info | email | * | \binfo@slint\.dev\b | upstream: the Slint licence contact
info | email | * | @kdab\.com\b | upstream: authors of the Slint sources the patch touches
info | email | driver/src/vivante/hw/*.xml.h | @ | upstream: authors of the etnaviv rules-ng headers
info | email | driver/src/v3d/* | \brobclark@freedesktop\.org\b | upstream: Mesa author of the code this file follows
info | email | tools/vivante/*.patch | @gmail\.com\b | upstream: etnaviv author in a Mesa patch
# Self-test fixtures of files held by other plans (their owners may drop the
# fixture instead; see docs/release/redaction-audit.md part 4).  One rule per
# value and exact path.  The names under .example and example.com are
# reserved (RFC 2606); the addresses are private-range inputs of a redaction
# or refusal test.
drop | email | tools/board_selftest.sh | tester[@]pi5-fake\.example\b | RFC 2606 .example fake BOARD_HOST of the pi5 dry-run self-test
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/board_selftest.sh | \b100\.64\.7\.9\b | private-range input of a redaction test: a fake ssh error that must be redacted
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/board_selftest.sh | \b10\.20\.30\.40\b | private-range input of a redaction test: console line that redact_run rewrites
drop | login-at-host | tools/board_selftest.sh | root[@]t6fake-host\b | fake BOARD_HOST of the NanoPC-T6 run self-test (a look-alike, never a real host): the test checks that no record carries it
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-slice-readme-selftest.sh | \b10\.1\.2\.3\b | private-range input of a refusal test: the slice check must refuse it
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/mali-slice-readme-selftest.sh | root[@]board\b | input of a refusal test: the slice check must refuse it
drop | email | tools/cts/x2-glmark2-scenes-selftest.sh | \bt[@]example\.com\b | RFC 2606 example.com git identity of the self-test repository
drop | home-path | tools/cts/mali-glmark2-selftest.sh | /ho[m]e/yakogl-mali-glmark2\b | the fake board's stage directory in a self-test, no user name
drop | home-path | tools/cts/mali-glmark2-session-selftest.sh | /ho[m]e/yakogl-mali-glmark2\b | the fake board's stage directory in a self-test, no user name
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-fail-triage.py | \b10\.1\.2\.3\b | private-range input of a redaction test (the scrub self-check)
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/mali-fail-triage.py | root[@]nano\b | input of a redaction test (the scrub self-check)
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/testdata/mali-fail-triage/slices/2026-11-09-t6-gles2-S1-11111111/kmsg/c.txt | \b10\.9\.8\.7\b | private-range input of a redaction test: a dirty kmsg line
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/testdata/mali-fail-triage/slices/2026-11-09-t6-gles2-S1-11111111/kmsg/c.txt | root[@]board\b | input of a redaction test: a dirty kmsg line
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/testdata/mali-slice-redact/dirty/kmsg/a.txt | root[@]board\b | input of a redaction test: a dirty kmsg line
drop | tailnet-dns | tools/cts/testdata/mali-slice-redact/dirty/meta.txt | \bboard-1\.example\.ts\.net\b | input of a redaction test under the reserved example name (RFC 2606)
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | \b100\.64\.0\.0\b | private-range input of a redaction test: the tailnet range in the tool's help
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | \b100\.64\.0\.9\b | private-range input of a redaction test: a tailnet address the check must report
drop | ipv6-local | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | \bfe80::1\b | link-local input of a redaction test
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | root[@]board\b | input of a redaction test
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | root[@]192\.0\.2\.7\b | input of a redaction test (RFC 5737 address)
drop | tailnet-dns | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | \bboard-1\.example\.ts\.net\b | input of a redaction test under the reserved example name (RFC 2606)
drop | email | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | serial-getty[@]ttyS2\.service\b | systemd unit instance in the tool's help, not an address
